WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.509
Wayfarer Airlines flight 515 was an important
part of the "Breaking Bad" mythology, a symbol

00:00:06.509 --> 00:00:09.910
of the horrible consequences of Walter White's
actions.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:15.559
His decision to let Jesse's girlfriend Jane
die leads to her father, an air traffic controller,

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:17.910
inadvertently causing a midair collision.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.920
The crash was subtly teased with black-and-white
prologues flashing forward to the disaster

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.689
all through the second season of "Breaking
Bad."

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:30.869
Saul Goodman milked the Wayfarer disaster
for all it was worth, wearing a memorial ribbon

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:33.790
on his lapel for the remainder of the "Breaking
Bad."

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:38.850
In The "Better Call Saul" series finale, he's
extradited back to New Mexico from Omaha to

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.559
plead guilty to his many crimes, flying with
a U.S. Marshal — and you can tell from the

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:45.890
seats it's a Wayfarer flight.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:50.950
Later, he enters the courtroom in a shiny
suit complete with his memorial ribbon still

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.140
pinned to the lapel.

